[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Waves]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.37]Lesson 40 | 第40课
[00:02.24]Waves | 海浪
[00:09.08]What false impression does an ocean wave convey to the observer? | 海浪给观察者造成了什么错误印象？
[00:15.37]Waves are the children of the struggle between ocean and atmosphere, the ongoing signatures of infinity. | 海浪是海洋与大气层斗争的产儿，是无限性永不停息的标记。
[00:23.26]Rays from the sun excite and energize the atmosphere of the earth, awakening it to flow, to movement, to rhythm, to life. | 太阳的射线激发并给地球的大气层以能量，唤醒它流动、运动、有节奏、有生命。
[00:33.29]The wind then speaks the message of the sun to the sea | 风于是把太阳的信息传给海洋，
[00:37.20]and the sea transmits it on through waves--an ancient, exquisite powerful message. | 而海洋又通过海浪把它继续传送下去——一个古老、精致而有力的信息。
[00:45.48]These ocean waves are among the earth's most complicated natural phenomena. | 这些海洋波浪属于地球上最复杂的自然现象。
[00:51.45]The basic features include a crest (the highest point of the wave), | 其基本特征包括波峰（波浪的最高点）、
[00:56.13]a trough (the lowest point), a height (the vertical distance from the trough to the crest), | 波谷（最低点）、波高（从波谷到波峰的垂直距离）、
[01:03.67]a wave length (the horizontal distance between two wave crests), | 波长（两个波峰之间的水平距离）、
[01:08.99]and a period (which is the time it takes awave crest to travel one wave length). | 以及周期（即一个波峰传播一个波长所需的时间）。
[01:16.21]Although an ocean wave gives the impression of a wall of water moving in your direction, | 尽管海浪给人的印象是朝你方向移动的一堵水墙，
[01:22.46]in actuality waves move through the water leaving the water about where it was. | 但实际上波浪在水中穿行而过，水却大致留在原处。
[01:29.36]If the water was moving with the wave, | 如果水是随着波浪移动的，
[01:32.06]the ocean and everything on it would be racing in to the shore with obviously catastrophic results. | 那么海洋以及海洋上的一切都会冲向海岸，其后果显然是灾难性的。
[01:40.03]An ocean wave passing through deep water causes a particle on the surface to move in a roughly circular orbit, | 深水中行进的海浪使水面上的一个质点沿大致圆形的轨道运动，
[01:48.49]drawing the particle first towards the advancing wave, then up into the wave, | 先把质点拉向行进中的波浪，然后向上送入波浪，
[01:54.41]then forward with it and then--as the wave leaves the particles behind--back to its starting point again. | 再随波浪向前，然后——当波浪把质点抛在后面时——又回到它的出发点。
[02:03.30]From both maturity to death, a wave is subject to the same laws as any other 'living' thing. | 从成熟到消亡，海浪同任何其他“有生命”的东西一样受同样的规律支配。
[02:10.15]For a time it assumes a miraculous individuality that, in the end, is reabsorbed into the great ocean of life. | 一时间，它呈现出不可思议的个性，而最终又被重新吸收进生命的海洋之中。
[02:19.11]The undulating waves of the open sea are generated by three natural causes: | 开阔海面的起伏波浪由三种自然力量产生：
[02:25.25]wind, earth movements or tremors, and the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun. | 风、地球的运动或震动，以及月亮和太阳的引力。
[02:31.95]Once waves have been generated, | 波浪一经产生，
[02:34.14]gravity is the force that drives them in a continual attempt to restore the ocean surface to a flat plain. | 重力便是驱使它们不断努力把海面恢复为平面的力量。
